Description: QuartzFire content filtering (e2guardian ICAP behind Squid ssl_bump)
 URL/domain/category filtering and content/phrase scanning for QuartzFire
 (VyOS-based NGFW), equivalent to WatchGuard Fireware's WebBlocker. e2guardian
 runs in ICAP SERVER mode only (no proxy, no MITM of its own): it listens on
 127.0.0.1:1344 and answers REQMOD/RESPMOD requests from the existing SSL
 Inspection Squid, which is the sole TLS terminator and the ICAP client. Squid
 bumps TLS first, so e2guardian filters already-decrypted plaintext.
 .
 A single Rust multi-call binary (qfcf) provides the `service content-filtering`
 conf-mode owner, the UT1 blocklist updater, the status plumbing the QuartzFire
 WebUI reads, and the URL-test facility. Filter groups map clients to policy by
 source IP; category filtering uses the UT1 (Université Toulouse) blocklists,
 layered under custom allow/block lists. The feature has a hard dependency on
 SSL Inspection — committing it without SSL inspection enabled is refused.
